{"lines": ["One more file. And this one is not a place, but a sickness.", "Between 1915 and 1926, an epidemic spread around the world. It was described in 1917 by the neurologists Constantin von Economo and Jean-Ren\u00e9 Cruchet. It was called encephalitis lethargica, or sleepy sickness.", "More than one million people were infected. More than five hundred thousand died.", "Many survivors were left statue-like, speechless and motionless.", "What caused it? It was once linked to the Spanish flu, but modern research argues against that. An enterovirus was found in cases. In 2012, Oliver Sacks, the author of Awakenings, acknowledged that virus as the probable cause. Other sources have suggested a bacterium, Streptococcus pneumoniae.", "In 2008, a review said that almost a hundred years later, the cause remained enigmatic.", "So here is the honest version. Known: a worldwide epidemic, more than five hundred thousand dead. Proposed: a virus. Unsolved: why it came, and why it vanished.", "Rule seven. Some mysteries stay open. Do not close one just because it is quiet."], "words": [["One", 0.0, 0.22], ["more", 0.22, 0.38], ["file.", 0.38, 0.76], ["And", 0.76, 1.14], ["this", 1.14, 1.3], ["one", 1.3, 1.54], ["is", 1.54, 1.74], ["not", 1.74, 1.92], ["a", 1.92, 2.0], ["place,", 2.0, 2.26], ["but", 2.26, 2.54], ["a", 2.54, 2.64], ["sickness.", 2.64, 2.92], ["Between", 3.9, 4.1], ["1915", 4.1, 4.66], ["and", 4.66, 5.52], ["1926,", 5.52, 6.32], ["an", 6.46, 7.12], ["epidemic", 7.12, 7.46], ["spread", 7.46, 7.92], ["around", 7.92, 8.22], ["the", 8.22, 8.4], ["world.", 8.4, 8.66], ["It", 9.26, 9.34], ["was", 9.34, 9.44], ["described", 9.44, 9.84], ["in", 9.84, 10.14], ["1917", 10.14, 10.98], ["by", 10.98, 11.76], ["the", 11.76, 11.86], ["neurologists", 11.86, 12.7], ["Constantin", 12.7, 13.36], ["von", 13.36, 13.58], ["Economo", 13.58, 14.24], ["and", 14.24, 14.66], ["Jean-Ren\u00e9", 14.66, 15.45], ["Cruchet.", 15.45, 16.24], ["It", 16.24, 16.34], ["was", 16.34, 16.44], ["called